  {
   "id": "concept1",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Capacitance"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "A capacitor is two conductors separated by an insulator (dielectric). Its capacitance is the charge stored per volt: $C = Q/V$, measured in farads; practical values are in µF, nF and pF. For parallel plates $C = ε_0 ε_r A/d$. The energy stored is $W = ½CV^2$.",
    "kn": "ಡೈಎಲೆಕ್ಟ್ರಿಕ್‌ನಿಂದ ಬೇರ್ಪಟ್ಟ ಎರಡು ವಾಹಕಗಳೇ ಧಾರಕ. ಧಾರಕತೆ C = Q/V, ಏಕಮಾನ ಫ್ಯಾರಡ್. ಸಮಾಂತರ ಫಲಕಗಳಿಗೆ C = ε0εrA/d. ಸಂಗ್ರಹಿತ ಶಕ್ತಿ W = ½CV²."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "C = Q/V; 1 µF = 10⁻⁶ F, 1 pF = 10⁻¹² F"
    },
    {
     "en": "C increases with A and εᵣ, decreases with d"
    },
    {
     "en": "W = ½CV²"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "A capacitor is two conductors separated by an insulator (dielectric). Its capacitance is the charge stored per volt: C = Q/V, measured in farads; practical values are in µF, nF and pF. For parallel plates C = ε_0 ε_r A/d. The energy stored is W = ½CV^2.",
    "kn": "ಡೈಎಲೆಕ್ಟ್ರಿಕ್‌ನಿಂದ ಬೇರ್ಪಟ್ಟ ಎರಡು ವಾಹಕಗಳೇ ಧಾರಕ. ಧಾರಕತೆ C = Q/V, ಏಕಮಾನ ಫ್ಯಾರಡ್. ಸಮಾಂತರ ಫಲಕಗಳಿಗೆ C = ε0εrA/d. ಸಂಗ್ರಹಿತ ಶಕ್ತಿ W = ½CV²."
   },
   "formula": "C = \\frac{\\varepsilon_0 \\varepsilon_r A}{d}, \\qquad W = \\tfrac12 CV^2"
  },
